---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const locale = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Why Kraal Code — Built for African Organisations"
  description="Kraal Code was designed from the ground up for East and Central African operating realities: multi-branch operations, mobile work, local compliance, and affordable pricing."
  locale={locale}
  canonicalUrl="https://kraalcode.com/en/why/"
>
  <section class="page-hero section--warm">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Why organisations choose Kraal Code</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-subtext">Kraal Code was not adapted from a system built for another market. It was designed from the ground up for how East and Central African organisations actually operate.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="why-grid">
        <div class="why-card">
          <h2>Affordable without being limited</h2>
          <p>From UGX 250,000 per month for your whole organisation — not per user. No implementation fees. No USD exchange rate surprises. Annual billing gives you 12 months for the price of 10.</p>
          <p>For a 30-user organisation, Kraal Code Professional costs UGX 1,000,000/month. The same size on Odoo Enterprise would cost approximately UGX 4,300,000/month — before implementation costs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <h2>Usable from day one</h2>
          <p>The Golden Rule: any employee should be able to complete core tasks on their first day without training. This is enforced by an 85% unassisted task success rate target across five benchmark tasks.</p>
          <p>Most ERP systems require weeks of training before anyone can use them productively. Kraal Code is designed so that the interface teaches itself.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <h2>Africa-native integrations</h2>
          <p>MTN MoMo, Airtel Money, M-Pesa, and EFRIS integrations are platform services — not afterthought add-ons. Mobile money salary disbursement, supplier payments, and customer receipts are built in.</p>
          <p>Localisation is configuration, not code. Adding a new country requires only a localisation profile with the right statutory rules, currency, and tax settings.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <h2>Serious about security</h2>
          <p>Tenant isolation, role-based access, immutable audit trails, AES-256 encryption, MFA, and OWASP Top 10 mapping. Security is not a footer badge — it is an architecture.</p>
          <p>Remote work, branch operations, and cloud access are only possible when you can trust the system to maintain accountability.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <h2>Modular growth</h2>
          <p>Start with six core modules. Add manufacturing, HR, projects, or AI intelligence when your organisation is ready. Every module shares the same data model and permission system.</p>
          <p>You do not need to replace your systems as you grow — Kraal Code grows with you.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <h2>Regional understanding</h2>
          <p>Built by a team that understands local business practices, regulatory requirements, and operating constraints. Multi-country statutory compliance for Uganda, Kenya, Tanzania, and Rwanda from launch.</p>
          <p>Support and implementation grounded in the region — not a help desk in another timezone.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--dark section">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <h2>See for yourself</h2>
      <p>The best way to understand Kraal Code is to see it running with your data, your workflows, and your team.</p>
      <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn btn--inverse">Request a Demonstration →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--kc-space-20) 0 var(--kc-space-12);
  }

  .page-hero h1 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-4xl);
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .page-hero-subtext {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-lg);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-4);
  }

  .why-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-8);
  }

  .why-card {
    padding: var(--kc-space-8);
    border: 1px solid var(--kc-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
  }

  .why-card h2 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-xl);
    font-family: var(--kc-font-body);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--kc-charcoal);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-4);
  }

  .why-card p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-3);
  }

  .why-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .btn--inverse {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--kc-space-4) var(--kc-space-8);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--kc-text-inverse);
    border: 2px solid var(--kc-teal-light);
    transition: all var(--kc-transition-fast);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-6);
  }

  .btn--inverse:hover {
    background: var(--kc-teal);
    border-color: var(--kc-teal);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .why-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .page-hero h1 { font-size: var(--kc-text-3xl); }
  }
</style>
